{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791281007,"nonce":"Av/30d9hR/TVMKu9BFnw6+MqqO0=","title":"Long bitmap natives hold up every collection while they run","message":"Ash stops all threads for a collection, and a thread inside a native call reaches the stop only when the call returns. blinc_abi's bitmap decode, resample, shrink and release are long pure-Rust calls and never marked themselves blocking (hl_blocking), so a collection started while Studio3D's worker was decoding or shrinking textures waited for them.\n\n**Measured** (Studio3D flight, Ash 10af36d, 2026-10-06): stop time during loading 46-233 ms of a 71-242 ms pause, mark under 10 ms. A sample of the first 7 s puts the worker in hl_blinc_bitmap_resample for about 1.7 s and hl_blinc_bitmap_decode for 0.3 s. Ash-side issue: 9ac60ec10f11e927aa4bba17a1b62aa9405beb48f6afb0377ee45cba8e93219d.\n\n**Fix:** those four natives run inside hl_blocking(true/false). They touch no GC object but the caller's byte buffers, and Ash's collector does not move objects. After: stop at most 6.6 ms, loading pauses at most 33 ms, over three runs.","files":null}]}